# Generated by deja stats --card, not part of the repo
deja-stats.svg

# Harness artefacts: running an agent inside this checkout to test an
# integration leaves its own history and config here. None of it belongs in
# the repository — three of these were committed by a careless `git add -A`.
.aider.chat.history.md
.aider.input.history
.aider.tags.cache.v*/
.grok/
.roo/
.cline/
.goose/
.opencode/
.qwen/
.kimi-code/

# One line per Go command under scripts/: `go build ./scripts/<name>` drops a
# binary called <name> in the repository root, and a careless `git add -A` then
# sweeps it into a commit — a 3.7 MB Mach-O reached main that way. Build probes
# with `-o /tmp/...` instead; these are the backstop for when someone forgets.
#
# Kept complete by `go run ./scripts/ignorecheck`, which CI runs. Before that
# this was two blocks that had drifted apart: seven names duplicated between
# them, seven packages with no line at all, and three lines for packages that no
# longer existed — while the comment above it said one line per package.
/corpusprobe
/day0bench
/decisionbench
/demo
/genlogo
/genmatrix
/genregistry
/harnesssweep
/ignorecheck
/indexnow
/locomo
/longmemeval
/mcpb
/mcpprobe
/miracl
/mkcorpus
/mockmodel
/pinmanifests
/planbench
/rankdiff
/relnotes
/reusebench
/searchbench

# Where story.py drops the film's frames when it is run without --out. Three
# hundred and twenty PNGs, one run.
/scripts/demo/frames/

# Python leaves these beside every script it runs, and there is Python in
# scripts/ and tools/. Nothing ignored them, so they were committable as
# binaries by anyone who ran one.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# extensions/ builds where its ecosystem builds: cargo in the Zed extension,
# npm in the two plugin packages. None of it is ours to commit.
extensions/zed/target/
extensions/zed/Cargo.lock
extensions/*/node_modules/
extensions/*/*.tgz
extensions/*/package-lock.json
